 summary=f"""# NHL Season 2026 hostile end-to-end readiness — one-page summary\n\nThe frozen {len(matrix)}-case matrix found six critical/high fail-open risks; all six received narrow semantic-preserving fixes and the full matrix passed afterward. Three medium operational issues remain: non-atomic interrupted writes require bounded cleanup, schema errors lack row-level diagnostics, and one SOG identity error blocks the slate.\n\nActual archived slates were frozen before testing: 2025-10-07, 2026-01-26, and 2026-03-14. Raw parsing is exact; intraday MIDDAY and FINAL_PREGAME states are explicitly bounded reconstructions. Full SOG parity covered 40,167 rows with maximum delta 5.83e-16 and zero material mismatches.\n\nMainline and SOG are ready for real preseason hostile validation, with manual operation only. Regular-season opening remains bounded by completion of real preseason evidence and the three medium issues. The one next task is `FIRST_REAL_NHL_SEASON_2026_PRESEASON_HOSTILE_VALIDATION`.\n"""
