 report="# NHL Season 2026 Hostile End-to-End Prospective Readiness Audit\n\n"+summary.split("\n",1)[1]+"\n## Evidence and limits\n\nNo outcomes informed slate selection or pregame reconstruction. Baseline synthetic end-to-end runs completed in both lanes; archived raw payloads parsed for all three slates, while exact intraday replay was not claimed. Create-only namespaces and manifests prevented cross-run and cross-lane mutation. MIDDAY and FINAL_PREGAME remained distinct. Grading was append-only. No wager, ROI, tuning, promotion, automation, or frontend action occurred.\n\nThe initially unsafe conditions were future quote capture, player/game mismatch, weak outcome run identity in both lanes, mainline slate mismatch, and unpinned frozen executable/model bytes. Regression fixtures now reject each before output finalization. Remaining medium defects are operational rather than silent contamination.\n\n## Decision\n\nBoth lanes: `READY_FOR_REAL_PRESEASON_HOSTILE_VALIDATION`. Shared substrate, recovery, and regular-season opening: `READY_WITH_BOUNDED_LIMITS`. Exactly one next task: `FIRST_REAL_NHL_SEASON_2026_PRESEASON_HOSTILE_VALIDATION`.\n"
